      "message": "The initial color can be used when a shader is set. \n1- A runtime shader can be declared as `half4 main(float2 coords, half4 color)` and this exposes the color directly.\n2- Even if the color isn\u0027t accessed directly, evaluating a null child shader will return the previous-stage color, which can be the initial color.\n\nHere\u0027s an example of the null child case that I just made: http://review.skia.org/580014",
